{
  "mesh": "humanoid-mannequin.glb",
  "meshSha256": "b2f33a51c4405c59f342abe6e9b7904db377c759d0a16c99cb444b2ba732c824",
  "skeleton": "Quaternius Rigify (Blender Rigify DEF-* bones), 53 bones, stripped-dot names as Three.js GLTFLoader sees them (DEF-thigh.L -> DEF-thighL)",
  "license": "CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain). Mesh source: Quaternius Universal Animation Library (Standard), Godot GLB build — https://store.godotengine.org/asset/quaternius/universal-animation-library/download/44/. Verbatim license in ../LICENSE-CC0-Quaternius.txt. All 16 clips hand-keyframed (no reused motion), so no additional license applies.",
  "sourceReview": "All 46 Quaternius clips reviewed by name (A_TPose, Crouch_Fwd/Idle_Loop, Dance_Loop, Death01, Driving_Loop, Fixing_Kneeling, Hit_Chest/Head, Idle_Loop/Talking/Torch_Loop, Interact, Jog_Fwd_Loop, Jump_Land/Loop/Start, PickUp_Table, Pistol_*, Punch_*, Push_Loop, Roll/Roll_RM, Sitting_*, Spell_Simple_*, Sprint_Loop, Swim_*, Sword_*, Walk_Formal_Loop, Walk_Loop). None genuinely matches any of the 16 movements: closest are Walk_Loop (a walk, not a lunge), Jump_Loop (vertical jump, not jumping jacks), Crouch_Fwd_Loop (crouch walk, not a squat). 0 reused, 16 hand-keyframed.",
  "method": "Hand-keyframed in Node + Three.js r187, same method as the PoC squat: world-space 2-bone IK for arms/legs (planted contact points where the movement has them), torso lean distributed over hips/spine, sampled at 30 fps, first frame == last frame (loop closure). Clip files are skeleton-only + one clip; props live in the mesh file per the asset contract. Plank is a static hold animated as a subtle breathing/settle loop (hips +/-1.5 cm, spine +/-1.5 deg), not a frozen pose. Walking lunge is in-place alternating (2 steps per loop) so the loop closes without the character travelling.",
  "props": "No props were added to any clip file (contract: clip files contain no meshes). Goblet squat and kettlebell swing are body-only: hands in a cupped/grip hold (fingers curled via finger tracks). A dumbbell/kettlebell prop parented to the hands would belong in the shared mesh file — not done here (mesh file untouched per brief).",
  "verification": {
    "method": "Headless Chromium (Playwright, SwiftShader WebGL) on this VM: loaded mesh GLB + each clip GLB, played the clip on the mesh with THREE.AnimationMixer, measured bone world positions, rendered 3 frames per clip (proof-lower/<id>_{t0,tmid,t75}.png). Node-side: loop closure (first vs last keyframe quat diff), reach audit (every end-effector target within limb length at every sampled frame), finite-value check on all track values.",
    "notVerifiedOnRealDevice": true,
    "note": "No real Android device was available on this VM. Phone-webview playback (Capacitor) is NOT yet verified — needs the app worker's on-device check, same as the PoC."
  },
